#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198398 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198040 :question/id #uuid "3fccb151-d67f-525b-8804-62589913084a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12407" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu = x+y^2, \\qquad\nv=  y+z, \\qquad\nw = 2z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\iiint \\limits_R (x+y^2)^{15}z \\: \\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\:  0 \\leq x+y^2 \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq y+z \\leq 4, \\: 0\\leq z\\leq 2 \\big\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}: {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{array} \\right]} \n\\longrightarrow \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x ( u , v , w ) \\\\ y ( u , v , w ) \\\\ z ( u , v , w )\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $\\Delta$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\ \\mathrm{d}V = \\iiint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ f(x(u,v,w), y(u,v,w), z(u,v,w)) \\: \\left| \\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)} \\right|  \\: \\textrm{d}u \\textrm{d}v \\textrm{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu = x+y^2, \\qquad\nv=  y+z, \\qquad\nw = 2z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function $\\mathbf T^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}^{-1}:{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array} \\right]} \\to {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u ( x , y , z ) \\\\ v ( x , y , z ) \\\\ w ( x , y , z )\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $\\Delta,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 4,\\,0\\le w\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf T^{-1}{:}$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf T^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf T{:}$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf T$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\partial (u, v, w)}{\\partial (x, y, z)} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)} \\neq 0$ everywhere inside $\\Delta.$ In other words, $\\mathbf{T}$ has no critical points inside $\\Delta.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+{y}^{2})^{15}z\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}{u}^{15}\\cdot \\frac{w}{2}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{∭}_{Δ}{u}^{15}w\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{u}^{15}w\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{15}\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}w\\,dw \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot [\\frac{{u}^{16}}{16}]_{u=0}^{u=1}\\cdot {[v]}_{v=0}^{v=4}\\cdot [\\frac{{w}^{2}}{2}]_{w=0}^{w=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{16}-0)\\cdot (4-0)\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "832dc2b8-873f-56c6-bd87-5e886a586fb1" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186730699 :question-generator/id #uuid "c6ded202-6bc1-5111-bb32-eebc95c384b4" :question-generator/script "generators/5d/5d714fe15b5409b2bd1de94d5f5d3c5f5c23b37edc30bc80305191acbf4aeeac/17592186198398.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f646c61-db32-5905-849a-04ada136657a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194370} {:answer/id #uuid "dda01489-76a5-59ec-9704-87adeb52fd5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194371} {:answer/id #uuid "18c290d7-6b8d-50ae-99c2-f0eb7045b012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194372} {:answer/id #uuid "1935b921-c755-5f9b-b2fd-fdf3102bd3a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194373} {:answer/id #uuid "494337ce-d303-53d0-97cd-b0e1b611d95e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f646c61-db32-5905-849a-04ada136657a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194370} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb5cc458-53cc-5d59-888b-d4167a5b9c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d5d9726-730c-531d-b668-66f3dda1040e" :question/math-academy-id "q-162139" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=3x-2y,\\,v=y+2z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(3x-2y)^{2}(y+2z)\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le 3x-2y\\le 3,\\,0\\le y+2z\\le 2,\\,0\\le 2z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=3x-2y,\\,v=y+2z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le 2,\\,0\\le w\\le \\frac{1}{2}\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(3x-2y)^{2}(y+2z)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}{u}^{2}v\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{u}^{2}v\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{u}^{2}\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}v\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1/2}dw \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}]}_{u=0}^{u=3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{v=0}^{v=2}\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (9-0)\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef7332e4-b981-54af-8da2-fcdb494e9902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197655} {:answer/id #uuid "281c6df6-036f-5860-be8c-11e9d432022a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197656} {:answer/id #uuid "7557b355-b5e6-5c35-9ec5-ce7baaeba82d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197658} {:answer/id #uuid "55d05532-6ff9-54f2-9d4c-bf3ea90714ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481979} {:answer/id #uuid "828f75f9-fca6-5a07-93ba-87dbb17ec87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef7332e4-b981-54af-8da2-fcdb494e9902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197655} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb66677-2e9a-5652-8302-63d8739cb7ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197654}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3982f9b1-ca56-5e4b-8f97-4f23fb6f2fc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-39055" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+y,\\,v=x+z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x+z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+y)\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le {x}^{2}+y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le x+z\\le 2,\\,-1\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+y,\\,v=x+z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le u\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le v\\le 2,\\,-1\\le w\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=-1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+y)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot |-1|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}v\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{-1}^{1}dw \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡u]_{u=\\pi /6}^{u=\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{v=0}^{v=2}\\cdot [w]_{w=-1}^{w=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374090 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83465347-83b5-56e1-942c-234dfe757ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374092} {:answer/id #uuid "612ab49b-15d8-51e5-aae7-a61849ec93f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374093} {:answer/id #uuid "a65ba9a5-15e7-5ad8-a491-1c88d583b06c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374094} {:answer/id #uuid "329bb962-4b70-560b-b47c-55ff92416c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374095} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb73704-113c-5943-812c-4fa342511784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "329bb962-4b70-560b-b47c-55ff92416c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374095} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2769a2e-b298-59d8-a66c-56d53b56460b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374091}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d79ae16-602a-5f97-985b-2aa915324df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161916" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+2y,\\,v=x-z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}({x}^{2}+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-z)\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le {x}^{2}+2y\\le 2,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le x-z\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\hspace{0.222em}-1\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+2y,\\,v=x-z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{Δ} & =\\{(u,v,w)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le u\\le 2,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\hspace{0.222em}-1\\le w\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $\\mathbf{T}$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}({x}^{2}+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-z)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{-1}^{1}dw \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]_{u=0}^{u=2}\\cdot {[\\operatorname{sin}⁡v]}_{v=0}^{v=\\pi /2}\\cdot [w]_{w=-1}^{w=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-0)\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (1-(-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374097 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bab9309-d8a5-51d1-807c-f4b9da8a32be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374099} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce54197-6e08-581c-ba9a-fae72f50566a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374100} {:answer/id #uuid "25b0799f-0058-5d49-9ffd-855eeeab2145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374101} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f508fc-00c9-564f-b3b2-26dd372c3765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374102} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6c269d-ee4e-5268-bed1-d76fc26084c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bab9309-d8a5-51d1-807c-f4b9da8a32be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374099} :answer-field/id #uuid "77c9eaf7-9a6d-5842-bcbc-caffd6461b49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374098}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18953d2e-5477-5ba3-a50e-218374e50b08" :question/math-academy-id "q-161917" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2x-y}{2},\\,v=\\frac{y}{2},\\,w=\\frac{z}{3}\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(\\frac{2x-y}{2}+\\frac{z}{3})\\,dV\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le \\frac{2x-y}{2}\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le \\frac{y}{2}\\le 2,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2x-y}{2},\\,v=\\frac{y}{2},\\,w=\\frac{z}{3}\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{Δ} & =\\{(u,v,w)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le u\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le v\\le 2,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le w\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,\\,\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=6.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $\\mathbf{T}$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(\\frac{2x-y}{2}+\\frac{z}{3})\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}(u+w)\\cdot |6|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(6u+6w)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[6uw+3{w}^{2}]_{w=0}^{w=1}\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6u(1-0)+3({1}^{2}-{0}^{2}))\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6u+3)\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6u+3)[v]_{v=0}^{v=2}\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6u+3)\\cdot 2\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(12u+6)\\,du \\\\  & =[6{u}^{2}+6u]_{u=0}^{u=1} \\\\  & =6({1}^{2}-{0}^{2})+6(1-0) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae83ac8f-234c-5acd-bbb5-b25a1cc99939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{3}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374127} {:answer/id #uuid "8b34f7d1-a718-5683-99cc-2aea4d235600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374128} {:answer/id #uuid "d20aea26-e03e-599a-8c57-858eaa89a312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{3}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374129} {:answer/id #uuid "eecb9e17-6350-5926-b72c-9db686768a31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{3}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374130} {:answer/id #uuid "c52a153b-0694-5e0b-973b-21e39ee2b46c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{3}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c52a153b-0694-5e0b-973b-21e39ee2b46c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{3}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374131} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5a98d3-da89-51a1-baff-f599217e67d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374126}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0352be10-03ed-5d12-9e9a-501335a3d9bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161929" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x+{y}^{2},\\,v=y+z,\\,w=2z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(y+z){e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le x+{y}^{2}\\le 3,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le y+z\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le z\\le 4\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+{y}^{2},\\,v=y+z,\\,w=2z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{Δ} & =\\{(u,v,w)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le u\\le 3,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le v\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le w\\le 8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $\\mathbf{T}$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(y+z){e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}v{e}^{u}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2}v{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}v{e}^{u}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{u}\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{8}dw \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{e}^{u}]_{u=0}^{u=3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3}-1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1b875c-d159-5d2e-8f13-b0a11a49b1dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374134} {:answer/id #uuid "d522bb1b-a6e0-542c-b287-0eb7cc75c928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374135} {:answer/id #uuid "d66c99b3-72d2-5b51-a1f5-0cf6426bc1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374136} {:answer/id #uuid "c566677a-3ae4-5a9b-809b-312542dd7afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374137} {:answer/id #uuid "c62d12ae-e78b-5b54-b6e4-3414b80f62a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c566677a-3ae4-5a9b-809b-312542dd7afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374137} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc458f63-8f78-5a90-bd9d-b73e6cf7b6dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374133}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f98ed60b-0dd5-5ecd-92ff-418213f8aa92" :question/math-academy-id "q-161931" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=2x+3y,\\,v=-2x+z,\\,w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+3y)\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le 2x+3y\\le 2\\pi ,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le -2x+z\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le z\\le 6\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2x+3y,\\,v=-2x+z,\\,w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{Δ} & =\\{(u,v,w)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le u\\le 2\\pi ,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le v\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le w\\le 3\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\,2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(-6)) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $\\mathbf{T}$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+3y)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}4{w}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{4}{3}{w}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}{w}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4{w}^{2}}{3}dw \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡u]_{u=\\pi /6}^{u=2\\pi }\\cdot {[v]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\cdot [\\frac{4{w}^{3}}{9}]_{w=0}^{w=3} \\\\  & =(0-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (12-0) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198c77be-33a4-5cbd-aa11-6bdd4191dd77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374141} {:answer/id #uuid "6556381a-7067-5b49-b676-6d3c5d67e172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374142} {:answer/id #uuid "9e51b078-3e9f-5dea-a9af-d596ee26bc5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374143} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfb13d8-becf-5996-837a-11efb07fcec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374144} {:answer/id #uuid "da79f3cb-6b50-5ceb-bf5c-54aa4f670f09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddfb13d8-becf-5996-837a-11efb07fcec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374144} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbb48d5b-5877-5dca-aa67-f0774b0d5c49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374140}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "954ec2ce-743f-514f-9ac4-50e6ba28f6e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161934" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+2y,\\,v=x-2z,\\,w=4z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-2z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le {x}^{2}+2y\\le \\pi ,\\hspace{0.222em}\\pi \\le x-2z\\le 2\\pi ,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+2y,\\,v=x-2z,\\,w=4z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{Δ} & =\\{(u,v,w)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le u\\le \\pi ,\\hspace{0.222em}\\pi \\le v\\le 2\\pi ,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le w\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${\\mathbf{T}}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(0-2) \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $\\mathbf{T}$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-2z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{8}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}dw \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u]_{u=\\pi /2}^{u=\\pi }\\cdot {[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v]}_{v=\\pi }^{v=2\\pi }\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(1+0)\\cdot (-1+(-1))\\cdot (4-0) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1536ecd2-34e1-5711-8194-9090d29369f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481834} {:answer/id #uuid "857fe175-09f7-5eb2-89ec-46c4061ca387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482087} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7b47f3-3802-5868-b5d4-8e9d5d18bbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482176} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a944d1-2a3f-544a-a5da-c1c851119eb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482198} {:answer/id #uuid "e454e28a-b46a-5bb3-81f3-e70638e4c982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab7b47f3-3802-5868-b5d4-8e9d5d18bbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482176} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5adb4bd-431e-53be-8fd6-9773762a903f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482489}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b7c4644-c6ca-51e8-b34c-e72d6ef6b667" :question/math-academy-id "q-161894" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x+y,\\,v=y+z,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\pi \\le x+y\\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le y+z\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+y,\\,v=y+z,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,\\pi \\le u\\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le w\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\cdot |-1|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}dw \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u]_{u=\\pi }^{u=2\\pi }\\cdot {[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v]}_{v=0}^{v=\\pi }\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=1} \\\\  & =(-1+(-1))\\cdot (-(-1)+1)\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13f0ef2e-0f93-5e0a-8d71-92286357a7c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481828} {:answer/id #uuid "2836c933-6423-5d47-b0d5-a225bde1662d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481878} {:answer/id #uuid "d2729257-14f7-5d82-bd92-97d5a5b741d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482278} {:answer/id #uuid "da0e5662-6a8a-576b-b15e-de600a9ace05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482294} {:answer/id #uuid "fe01dfce-1c89-5728-a40a-4b936e3d1215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2836c933-6423-5d47-b0d5-a225bde1662d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481878} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0305ffe-7471-5805-bce3-ea016f3e92ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482486}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8c9e8ae-5eea-50e8-acfe-85f90d5a9922" :question/math-academy-id "q-161933" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=y+z,\\,v=x+4z,\\,w=2y\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\,\\frac{y+z}{x+4z}\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y+z\\le 2,\\,1\\le x+4z\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=y+z,\\,v=x+4z,\\,w=2y\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,1\\le v\\le e,\\,0\\le w\\le 2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-1)(-1). \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{y+z}{x+4z}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{v}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{2v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{u}{2v}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{u}{2}\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{v}\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}dw \\\\  & =[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{4}]_{u=0}^{u=2}\\cdot {[\\operatorname{ln}⁡v]}_{v=1}^{v=e}\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=2} \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ee0c1d0-b902-5d6e-9fd8-7baec2f61f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481859} {:answer/id #uuid "572c02e1-9d71-5b99-960a-6f12882be763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481981} {:answer/id #uuid "70ef93b1-e501-54d3-bcff-1f06883cd750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482035} {:answer/id #uuid "75475609-dfeb-560d-bc22-9379064434fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482047} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5aafc8-ceba-5678-a412-98f1f904e581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ee0c1d0-b902-5d6e-9fd8-7baec2f61f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481859} :answer-field/id #uuid "3587c6f6-e4fb-567f-a4f3-80de70f97f45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482407}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e662cc33-8ce5-5a82-9731-097b3595e6c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-162140" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x+{y}^{2},\\,v=y+z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x+{y}^{2})^{9}z\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x+{y}^{2}\\le 1,\\,0\\le y+z\\le 5,\\,0\\le z\\le 4\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+{y}^{2},\\,v=y+z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 5,\\,0\\le w\\le 2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+{y}^{2})^{9}z\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}{u}^{9}w\\cdot |1|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{u}^{9}w\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{u}^{9}w\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{9}\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{5}dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}w\\,dw \\\\  & =[\\frac{{u}^{10}}{10}]_{u=0}^{u=1}\\cdot {[v]}_{v=0}^{v=5}\\cdot [\\frac{{w}^{2}}{2}]_{w=0}^{w=4} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{10}-0)\\cdot (5-0)\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1784c964-2bd8-551a-9e62-6cb6f2560ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498780} {:answer/id #uuid "255b1548-0862-5d3a-8e4b-d22ea5aa0f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498812} {:answer/id #uuid "4f74f069-41cb-54fc-8a9a-08d22d7c1865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498916} {:answer/id #uuid "7d9780c4-afc1-59e7-ac65-84b80ad23ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499011} {:answer/id #uuid "903bd708-b320-50fc-b991-e52faae4df28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d9780c4-afc1-59e7-ac65-84b80ad23ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499011} :answer-field/id #uuid "2030cf44-2880-55da-b8da-7f5dffbc7894" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499324}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "787730fc-5924-57cd-ac3a-f6e87e085583" :question/math-academy-id "q-161893" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x+y,\\,v=y-x,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n∭(x+y){e}^{y-x}\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x+y\\le 2,\\,0\\le y-x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+y,\\,v=y-x,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le w\\le 3\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+y){e}^{y-x}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}u{e}^{v}\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{u{e}^{v}}{2}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{u{e}^{v}}{2}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}u\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{v}\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}dw \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]_{u=1}^{u=2}\\cdot {[{e}^{v}]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (e-1)\\cdot (3-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dbc4c08-f008-5e72-b85a-8f2b4179ee34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522152} {:answer/id #uuid "4cfefb36-0c70-50b6-aa6a-4945530149e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522185} {:answer/id #uuid "97e3dd6a-5cc0-5fa9-95f1-4e769dfdd8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522330} {:answer/id #uuid "c921974f-fc45-5558-acc3-f2310130ec21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522438} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8b09ec-156b-5830-8ce7-eac0fbd892c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97e3dd6a-5cc0-5fa9-95f1-4e769dfdd8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522330} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00110c2-7288-57e8-9508-75b52e302e96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522666}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c40cfd48-e992-514e-93b1-f5d1aa09838d" :question/math-academy-id "q-162128" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=2x+y,\\,v=3x+2z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{12}{1+(3x+2z)^{2}}\\,dV,\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\le 2x+y\\le \\frac{2}{\\pi },\\,\\,0\\le 3x+2z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2x+y,\\,v=3x+2z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\le u\\le \\frac{2}{\\pi },\\,0\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le w\\le 2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{12}{1+(3x+2z)^{2}}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{12}{1+{v}^{2}}\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{3}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{4}{(1+{v}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/\\pi }^{2/\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4}{(1+{v}^{2})}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/\\pi }^{2/\\pi }\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4}{(1+{v}^{2})}\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}dw \\\\  & =[u]_{1/\\pi }^{2/\\pi }\\cdot {[4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡v]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{\\pi })\\cdot (4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}-0)\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541281 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a249df-c9f4-5dec-b4de-f9ba0746d97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541280} {:answer/id #uuid "26ae7e04-d8af-5bb6-8f2d-43c43c7f28f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541288} {:answer/id #uuid "5d351302-9c8c-543f-9145-afcb9c6f9577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541307} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2bc279-f829-52c9-8684-578e789779f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541309} {:answer/id #uuid "f737d865-02df-5cc1-a11b-d003929e5c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ae7e04-d8af-5bb6-8f2d-43c43c7f28f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541288} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d0db58-1db4-5743-8659-a051cf062d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541329}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "173b6f27-e7f0-5312-9952-6882bf4ed1e5" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=2 x + y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(2 x + y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):0\\le 2 x + y\\le 2,\\quad 0\\le y + 2 z\\le 2,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2 x + y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):0\\le u\\le 2,\\quad 0\\le v\\le 2,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 6\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(2\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(2 x + y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u v\\right)\\cdot \\left|\\frac{1}{6}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\int_{0}^{2}\\int_{0}^{6}\\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v w}{6}\\right]_{w=0}^{w=6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(6\\right)}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(0\\right)}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\left(u v\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(u v\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v^{2}}{2}\\right]_{v=0}^{v=2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(2\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\left(2 u\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(2 u\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[u^{2}\\right]_{u=0}^{u=2} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(2\\right)^{2}\\right)-\\left(\\left(0\\right)^{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(4\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25e7eb24-fc02-5f52-9c20-aae50650f4a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541287} {:answer/id #uuid "29af25a0-b38c-56b0-be84-926f09256318" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541291} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7c1988-b4dc-5569-aa90-8360768fae64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541296} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1d065e-c0c0-5bd0-86fb-b8aca3ae9250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{243}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541312} {:answer/id #uuid "7f1c4b97-5aa6-5e63-baf9-19b1c025a22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25e7eb24-fc02-5f52-9c20-aae50650f4a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541287} :answer-field/id #uuid "18ec8df9-6aac-54db-9e1e-7c3583337cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541283}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "288adffb-1495-599b-84c2-f5316cf5e72b" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=- 3 x - y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x - y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):0\\le - 3 x - y\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le y + 2 z\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=- 3 x - y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):0\\le u\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le v\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(-3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(-1\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{9}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x - y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u v\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{9}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u v}{9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\frac{u v}{9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v w}{9}\\right]_{w=0}^{w=3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(3\\right)}{9}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(0\\right)}{9}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{u v}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v^{2}}{6}\\right]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\frac{u}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{2}}{12}\\right]_{u=0}^{u=3} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{\\left(3\\right)^{2}}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "558c003d-194c-50a3-afd9-3b3c49be6773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541299} {:answer/id #uuid "5793a4c8-0967-5ecf-bc06-c983693ff7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541302} {:answer/id #uuid "5a0da766-41f2-5b2c-8d6f-6a7f1874052f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541303} {:answer/id #uuid "7a414439-4411-5e19-86bb-89d25e2b50ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541314} {:answer/id #uuid "8c441f4c-3be9-5350-921e-3e75864520c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{243}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5793a4c8-0967-5ecf-bc06-c983693ff7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541302} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f2d6119-6062-59dd-87d0-10fbb48f1490" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541285}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d58106b-6575-5f8d-b378-a90d367a817e" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=- 3 x - y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x - y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):0\\le - 3 x - y\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le y + 2 z\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=- 3 x - y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):0\\le u\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le v\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 6\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(-3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(-1\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{9}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x - y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u v\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{9}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u v}{9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{6}\\left(\\frac{u v}{9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v w}{9}\\right]_{w=0}^{w=6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(6\\right)}{9}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(0\\right)}{9}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{2 u v}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2 u v}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v^{2}}{3}\\right]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\frac{u}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{2}}{6}\\right]_{u=0}^{u=3} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{\\left(3\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18765fe5-128b-5142-9236-a3a46d45a15c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{52}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541282} {:answer/id #uuid "3b47c2ca-f0bd-56f2-bf5e-2bcf0cddf7b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "312" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541292} {:answer/id #uuid "5de3fc41-5f2d-5a8e-aac6-a9fab9a43655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541308} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ab7925-7495-51e7-9ff1-6521bd68a453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541337} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ad2699-dd25-5fb2-84bd-466354b5296f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2ad2699-dd25-5fb2-84bd-466354b5296f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541343} :answer-field/id #uuid "5606f3d8-e847-5048-bb67-787d18f89afc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541301}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5aa7bd83-f04d-5994-9b11-f8781cd4d34f" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=3 x + 2 y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(3 x + 2 y\\right)^{2} \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):1\\le 3 x + 2 y\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le y + 2 z\\le 2,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=3 x + 2 y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):1\\le u\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le v\\le 2,\\quad 2\\le w\\le 6\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(2\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(3 x + 2 y\\right)^{2} \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u^{2} v\\right)\\cdot \\left|\\frac{1}{6}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u^{2} v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{2}^{6}\\left(\\frac{u^{2} v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u^{2} v w}{6}\\right]_{w=2}^{w=6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u^{2} v \\left(6\\right)}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u^{2} v \\left(2\\right)}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(u^{2} v\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u^{2} v}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\frac{2 u^{2} v}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u^{2} v^{2}}{3}\\right]_{v=1}^{v=2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u^{2} \\left(2\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u^{2} \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{4 u^{2}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u^{2}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(u^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{3}}{3}\\right]_{u=1}^{u=3} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{\\left(3\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(9\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04657d2c-3ddb-58d1-9d67-dd10a54dc0b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{405}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541275} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab741f5-f47f-55dd-a3f0-ae63f69ddbb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541315} {:answer/id #uuid "901cc91b-26fc-5a1b-8456-c52a31fb8741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541319} {:answer/id #uuid "a1296fd9-7fec-5bcf-b59f-60a598631cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541327} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8421fb-677c-5f7e-b1a8-c484662b9b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ab741f5-f47f-55dd-a3f0-ae63f69ddbb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541315} :answer-field/id #uuid "19ba0a22-e819-5244-a80b-71a49791ee76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541284}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9650f3e3-cc32-52c0-a0d3-827c40cd5abf" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 3 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x + 2 z\\right) \\cos{\\left(x^{2} + 3 y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le x^{2} + 3 y\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 1\\le x + 2 z\\le 4,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 3 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le u\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 1\\le v\\le 4,\\quad 3\\le w\\le 9\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)-\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{9}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x + 2 z\\right) \\cos{\\left(x^{2} + 3 y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{9}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{3}^{9}\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(\\left[\\frac{v w \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{9}\\right]_{w=3}^{w=9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(\\left(\\frac{v \\left(9\\right) \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{9}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{v \\left(3\\right) \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{9}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(\\left(v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(\\frac{2 v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left[\\frac{v^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{v=1}^{v=4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(4\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left(\\frac{16 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(5 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[5 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\  & =\\left(5 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)}\\right)-\\left(5 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(5\\right)-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cac0cfd-8c08-5693-8241-6ca20d9e2a35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541297} {:answer/id #uuid "6757bd50-9e6f-5dd8-a9f2-cedca3d927b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541311} {:answer/id #uuid "98bec14f-3a08-5435-93a8-37c729d5ad2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541322} {:answer/id #uuid "ee26e376-13fa-58e3-8df2-d79974758cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541341} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb45e08-511b-5b14-94c9-f0ceacb890e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeb45e08-511b-5b14-94c9-f0ceacb890e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541342} :answer-field/id #uuid "addb0864-1aef-5c00-9c38-d91ca6be4e91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541331}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a23caed0-b0d6-5bc7-85a1-57147c01f56c" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=3 x - 2 y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(3 x - 2 y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):0\\le 3 x - 2 y\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le y + 2 z\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=3 x - 2 y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):0\\le u\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le v\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(-2\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(3 x - 2 y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u v\\right)\\cdot \\left|\\frac{1}{6}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{4}\\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v w}{6}\\right]_{w=0}^{w=4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(4\\right)}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(0\\right)}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{2 u v}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\frac{2 u v}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v^{2}}{3}\\right]_{v=0}^{v=3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(3\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(3 u\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(3 u\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{3 u^{2}}{2}\\right]_{u=0}^{u=1} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3 \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3 \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d7f614-2d0d-5b4f-8a4d-5a430e668c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541277} {:answer/id #uuid "152b9c08-7c4c-5e4f-a8bf-bbdc2a3842c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541279} {:answer/id #uuid "24a04031-d6cc-50a4-b638-5f6376be444c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541286} {:answer/id #uuid "5a177f47-6fb8-5c2f-9bfa-96bcc20a72cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541304} {:answer/id #uuid "5d07125f-13b1-5f8d-a78d-d9b4fa23d612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24a04031-d6cc-50a4-b638-5f6376be444c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541286} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccb3f74c-54d7-51d7-81f2-a0054fada802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541335}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5692f69-3609-5609-944f-4e446bbb7794" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=- 3 x + 2 y,\\quad v=y - 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x + 2 y\\right) \\left(y - 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):0\\le - 3 x + 2 y\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le y - 2 z\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=- 3 x + 2 y,\\quad v=y - 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):0\\le u\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le v\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(-3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(2\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x + 2 y\\right) \\left(y - 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u v\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{6}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v w}{6}\\right]_{w=0}^{w=2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(2\\right)}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(0\\right)}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{u v}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v^{2}}{6}\\right]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{u}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{2}}{12}\\right]_{u=0}^{u=1} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{12}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45c2c794-fa96-56ee-897b-6a7924f729cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541294} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7079ae-ca07-5029-bed0-98bf2758279f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541310} {:answer/id #uuid "7f871f55-3848-58d1-87a9-105664f12da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541317} {:answer/id #uuid "9af31736-01f8-5259-af4f-3db984201269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541325} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a62cf9-6bf3-5fb6-8756-053287095ab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{3} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e7079ae-ca07-5029-bed0-98bf2758279f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541310} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f004d4f-3fc8-5712-bdb7-94250c20150d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541278}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cbecea42-79f4-5eda-a847-bcaa6ee8d720" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x^{2} + 4 y\\right) \\cos{\\left(x + 2 z \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):1\\le x^{2} + 4 y\\le 3,\\quad \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le x + 2 z\\le 2 \\pi,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):1\\le u\\le 3,\\quad \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le v\\le 2 \\pi,\\quad 3\\le w\\le 9\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)-\\left(4\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x^{2} + 4 y\\right) \\cos{\\left(x + 2 z \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{12}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{3}^{9}\\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u w \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right]_{w=3}^{w=9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(9\\right) \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(3\\right) \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{v=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{v=2 \\pi}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\sin{\\left(\\left(2 \\pi\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(0\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- \\frac{u}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[- \\frac{u^{2}}{8}\\right]_{u=1}^{u=3} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\left(3\\right)^{2}}{8}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{9}{8}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076da802-ebd4-5da6-989d-b4e5ee107e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541276} {:answer/id #uuid "41536c9e-e5b7-5db2-82d2-6457fa4bfb50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541293} {:answer/id #uuid "946eea59-cb39-5110-93da-4da8429496e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541320} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9c3439-8be9-5d70-9591-b114a9dd46ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541323} {:answer/id #uuid "a7eb6120-e06c-502b-a15a-ded7ad89fd3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "946eea59-cb39-5110-93da-4da8429496e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541320} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac30ff6-c4fa-56e7-b428-f1de8fca1721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541324}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e65aaa3c-bfef-550f-8cdc-5c5c2d6c14c5" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x + 2 z\\right) \\cos{\\left(x^{2} + 4 y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le x^{2} + 4 y\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 1\\le x + 2 z\\le 2,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le u\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 1\\le v\\le 2,\\quad 3\\le w\\le 9\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)-\\left(4\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x + 2 z\\right) \\cos{\\left(x^{2} + 4 y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{12}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{3}^{9}\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left[\\frac{v w \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right]_{w=3}^{w=9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{v \\left(9\\right) \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{v \\left(3\\right) \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left[\\frac{v^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{v=1}^{v=2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(2\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left(\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274826f8-5ee6-5553-bcdf-f924e9e3dc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541289} {:answer/id #uuid "45f790a6-5bdd-5a23-8e33-6514f21d7fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541295} {:answer/id #uuid "75202ae0-10b9-5c01-86bc-851a32c37874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541313} {:answer/id #uuid "9cdf4172-38bd-54c7-b0af-051c53b46cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541326} {:answer/id #uuid "d448f991-6e4c-5057-88e8-e3ae71348076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75202ae0-10b9-5c01-86bc-851a32c37874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541313} :answer-field/id #uuid "55e464bd-ee58-52ed-a62f-e6330cc3a34a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541300}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed8bddf2-150b-5447-8fa1-d8697f536efc" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - \\frac{y}{4},\\quad v=\\frac{y}{4},\\quad w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(x - \\frac{y}{4} + \\frac{z}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):1\\le x - \\frac{y}{4}\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le \\frac{y}{4}\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - \\frac{y}{4},\\quad v=\\frac{y}{4},\\quad w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):1\\le u\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le v\\le 3,\\quad \\frac{1}{2}\\le w\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - \\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=8.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(x - \\frac{y}{4} + \\frac{z}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u + w\\right)\\cdot \\left|8\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(8 u + 8 w\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}\\left(8 u + 8 w\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left[8 u w + 4 w^{2}\\right]_{w=\\frac{1}{2}}^{w=1}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(4 \\left(1\\right)^{2}\\right)-\\left(4 \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2}\\right)+\\left(8 u \\left(1\\right)\\right)-\\left(8 u \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(4\\right)-\\left(1\\right)+\\left(8 u\\right)-\\left(4 u\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(4 u + 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left[v \\left(4 u + 3\\right)\\right]_{v=1}^{v=3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(3 \\left(3\\right)\\right)-\\left(3 \\left(1\\right)\\right)+\\left(4 u \\left(3\\right)\\right)-\\left(4 u \\left(1\\right)\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(9\\right)-\\left(3\\right)+\\left(12 u\\right)-\\left(4 u\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(8 u + 6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[4 u^{2} + 6 u\\right]_{u=1}^{u=3} \\\\  & =\\left(4 \\left(3\\right)^{2}\\right)-\\left(4 \\left(1\\right)^{2}\\right)+\\left(6 \\left(3\\right)\\right)-\\left(6 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(36\\right)-\\left(4\\right)+\\left(18\\right)-\\left(6\\right) \\\\  & =44\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using a Change of Variables"}]}
